A||||3||theogre||Wheel Locks||||10||
Z||000000||theogre||04-13-2000||02:22 PM||||For those who still want to retain the factory lugs and plastic caps but want/need new wheel locks.<P>McGard has locks for Fiero that accept the GM plastic lug caps. These are more readily available than the ones that came as a factory option. (You can get the originals replaced thru pontiac or directly from the maker. You can also get new keys if you want.)<P>The McGard part number is 24012. (12x1.5 threads) A set is around 20$us and includes one key.||||reg||10
Z||000001||Raydar||04-13-2000||05:01 PM||||Ogre, Thanks! Good info.<BR>That's way up on my list of "stuff to do".||||reg||14
Z||000002||BOILERMAKER||04-13-2000||08:01 PM||||I haven't heard of McGard.  Is there a webpage or is that a local store in most cities.||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||04-13-2000||08:19 PM||||McGard is very well known. They are one of 2 companies that supply most of the locks used by GM, I belive Ford and Chrysler as well.<P>They are available thru better tire stores, PepBoys and other places.<P>McGard locks are far better than nearly every other brand. For one thing the chromed ones don't rust or flake. Even after repeated removals. The key is not likely to strip even when used in air tools. (((NEVER USE AIR TOOLS ON WHEEL LOCKS!)))<P>McGard's only real competition is the company that makes the OEM ones on Fiero. ((I have the notes who that is someplace. It's also listed on one of the club web sites, and maybe FOSG.)||||reg||1
